  "passage": "Greenfield High School's Science Week was a great success! On Monday, we had a workshop on weather. Students learned about thunderstorms and how lightning forms. Using a mobile weather station, we recorded data during a real thunderstorm that hit our town. It was uncomfortable to stand in the rain and wind, but the experience was valuable for our projects. On Tuesday, we focused on farming and sustainability. We discussed how a quarter of the world's food comes from small farms, and why it's important to support them. In biology class, we used textbooks to study marine life, and some students even tried diving in the school's new pool to see underwater plants. The week ended with a record attempt for the longest science experiment, which lasted three hours. Everyone agreed it was an excellent way to learn new things and have fun.",
